### `description-title-case`

Check English package titles against [R's `tools::toTitleCase()`](https://search.r-project.org/R/refmans/tools/html/toTitleCase.html), with CRAN's additional exemption for single-quoted software names. R's stopwords, technical terms, mixed-case names, and capitalization after punctuation determine the suggested title.

This rule is **off by default** because technical names and editorial choices often need exceptions. Enable it with `--select description-title-case`. It checks titles when `Language` is absent, `en`, or starts with `en-`. Missing or empty titles and titles equal to the package name are left to other rules, matching CRAN's gating.

There is no autofix: the author must decide which capitalization suits the package and its software names.

This rule is **disabled by default**; enable it with `select`.

Capitalize principal words while preserving stopwords:

```text
Package: mypkg
Title: Statistical methods for data analysis
```

```text
warning: description-title-case
 --> DESCRIPTION:2:8
  |
2 | Title: Statistical methods for data analysis
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the `Title` field should use English title case
  = help: Consider: Statistical Methods for Data Analysis
```

Preserve the spelling of quoted software names:

```text
Package: mypkg
Title: fitting models with 'mixed-effects software'
```

```text
warning: description-title-case
 --> DESCRIPTION:2:8
  |
2 | Title: fitting models with 'mixed-effects software'
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the `Title` field should use English title case
  = help: Consider: Fitting Models with 'mixed-effects software'
```
